  "body": "### What happened\n\nI exported a STEP file from Fusion which used inch units. Upon import in CamCraft, the model was scaled very small. It appeared to be assuming the units of the file were in mm.\n\nAfter changing the document units to mm in Fusion and then re-exporting, the file was scaled correctly in CamCraft.\n\nI think CamCraft is ignoring the `CONVERSION_BASED_UNIT('inch',#2809)` line in the STEP file\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Export model from Fusion with inch units\n2. Import into CamCraft\n3. Model is 25.4x too small\n\n### camcraft version and OS\n\nBuilt from latest main on Linux, commit `034e91b8b78fa64989d18e1d5d17344531c4762c`\n\n### Screenshots or recording\n\n<img width=\"1434\" height=\"810\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e08fa42a-597a-400f-9c19-2e892b3b46e0\" />\n\nStock set to the expected size of the model. Model is too small.",
